Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: re-apply and if needed re-read the EDID in get_modes

msm_dp_panel_get_modes() relies on the connector EDID set at HPD time. With
a USB-C dock, HPD flips around the USB-PD power/data role swaps and
userspace can probe while the connector EDID is cleared, getting no modes
and falling back to 640x480 (seen on a OnePlus 7 Pro with a JSAUX dock and
a 3440x1440 monitor; the same dock reported full modes on other attaches).

Re-apply the EDID we hold before adding modes, and read it again once over
AUX if that still yields none.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c	2026-11-13 21:43:56.471525005 +0100
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c	2026-11-13 21:43:56.482415211 +0100
@@ -324,8 +324,28 @@
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
-	if (msm_dp_panel->drm_edid)
-		return drm_edid_connector_add_modes(connector);
+	if (msm_dp_panel->drm_edid) {
+		struct msm_dp_panel_private *panel =
+			container_of(msm_dp_panel, struct msm_dp_panel_private, msm_dp_panel);
+		int count;
+
+		/*
+		 * The connector's EDID is set at HPD time; HPD flips around
+		 * USB-PD role swaps can leave it cleared when userspace probes,
+		 * which reports no modes and falls back to 640x480. Re-apply the
+		 * EDID we hold, and read it again once if that gives no modes.
+		 */
+		drm_edid_connector_update(connector, msm_dp_panel->drm_edid);
+		count = drm_edid_connector_add_modes(connector);
+		if (count > 0)
+			return count;
+
+		drm_edid_free(msm_dp_panel->drm_edid);
+		msm_dp_panel->drm_edid = drm_edid_read_ddc(connector, &panel->aux->ddc);
+		drm_edid_connector_update(connector, msm_dp_panel->drm_edid);
+		if (msm_dp_panel->drm_edid)
+			return drm_edid_connector_add_modes(connector);
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
